To write a C++ function that takes a reference to a `std::string` containing markdown formatted text and returns a `std::string` containing HTML formatted text, you can use a library like `markdown-cpp`. First, include the necessary headers and link the `markdown-cpp` library. Then, define the function:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <markdown-cpp/markdown.h>

std::string markdownToHtml(const std::string& markdownText) {
    markdown::Markdown md;
    std::string htmlText = md.convert(markdownText);
    return htmlText;
}

int main() {
    std::string markdownText = "This is a test";
    std::string htmlText = markdownToHtml(markdownText);
    std::cout << htmlText << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```

